silm:instances_papers_21_ologs_and_typed_english_chapters_02_typed_noun_discipline_sections_03_bare_noun_cheese_trap_concrete_anchor_3_bare_milk#massnounrejected silm:hasLongDescription "The MassNounRejected is the mass noun 'milk' (uncountable), rejected by tau_N. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'bare_milk', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
